{"id": "daa15c4b-c52d-4a15-8756-117c66547a2a", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T20:53:47.281572", "source": "user", "parent_id": "6a7d6219-2216-4080-9f50-630d38c2333d", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Please perform an initial inspection and propose an approach for designing an experiment that answers: 'Will chain-of-thought (CoT) prompting improve the task-solving ability of LLM-based agents in WorkArena++?' At this stage, do NOT produce the full design or run anything; execution is not required for this design-only deliverable. Specifically report back with the following sections (compact but concrete): 1) **Repository / context inspection**: list what is available under /workspace (or note that it is empty or inaccessible given the bubblewrap environment with network disabled). Identify any WorkArena++, BrowserGym, or agent-framework artifacts already present, and any dataset/task lists referenced. Note relevant versions if visible. 2) **Key setup assumptions that need confirmation**, covering at minimum: (a) the LLM backbone(s) to compare (e.g., one open model vs. one frontier API), (b) the prompting conditions (zero-shot baseline vs. zero-shot + CoT, and whether self-consistency / few-shot CoT is in scope), (c) the WorkArena++ subset and task count (full benchmark vs. a representative stratified subset), (d) agent loop / action space (BrowserGym default vs. custom), (e) number of trials per task and seed handling, (f) evaluation metrics (success rate, step count, cost), (g) any human-validators or LLM-judges used in the original benchmark. 3) **Proposed high-level approach**: skeleton of the experimental design (conditions, independent/dependent variables, controls, randomization, statistical test, and how causality for 'CoT helps' would be argued). Distinguish choices that are source-supported vs. choices you are proposing as assumptions. 4) **Consequential assumptions and uncertainties**: list at least the items in the project's 'unknowns' (expected empirical outcome, unstated resources / runtime budget, missing setup details) plus any additional risks you see (prompt leakage, contamination, evaluator variability, model API non-determinism). Do not fabricate benchmark numbers or prior results; if you cite typical ranges from prior WorkArena / BrowserGym papers, mark them as unverified and source them only from documents present in scope. End your reply with a short numbered list of the top clarifications you need from the researcher before drafting the final design.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Will the chain-of-thought (CoT) prompting mechanism improve the task-solving ability of LLM-based agents in WorkArena++?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/97713/3:setup_1\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
