{"id": "c1c01542-1c8f-45e0-877b-6e6577b06731", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T20:54:39.732652", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "45cfdd19-37cc-42a6-90fe-83f1ef887738", "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "## 1) Repository / context inspection\n- **`/workspace`**: contains exactly one file — `task.json`. No `track.md`, no papers, no code, no datasets on disk; no artifact under any of `workarena*`, `browsergym*`, `agentlab*` was found by a top-3 filesystem sweep.\n- **`task.json` documents`**: lists only `track.md` with the note *\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"* — corroborating that this turn produces a design, not a run.\n- **Runtime**: bubblewrap, no network, Python 3.12.3, no agent/LLM/Playwright SDKs installed. Only `requests` is present in user site-packages.\n- **Referenced researcher topic** `neurips2024/97713/3:setup_1` is **not materialized** anywhere in `/workspace`; treat its contents as **out of scope / unavailable** unless the researcher pastes the relevant text. I will not infer items from it.\n- **Net consequence for the design**: every concrete prior-work fact (WorkArena++ task count, L1/L2/L3 split, baseline success-rate ranges, exact BrowserGym version, official CoT prompting template, evaluator type) **cannot be cited in-scope**. Each will be either researcher-confirmed or carried as an explicit assumption.\n\n## 2) Key setup assumptions that need confirmation\nFor each, I mark source-supported (none, given the empty repo) vs. proposed assumption.\n| # | Item | Proposed default (assumption, not source-supported) | Needs researcher confirmation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| a | **LLM backbones** | One open model (e.g., a Llama-3.x 8B/70B instruct via a self-hosted endpoint, since no GPU is provisioned in this bubblewrap) **and** one frontier API (e.g., GPT-4o-class or Claude-class). Both run under identical prompts/loop. | Which exact model IDs? API key availability? GPU/runtime budget (none currently)? |\n| b | **Prompting conditions** | Primary 2×1: `zero-shot` vs. `zero-shot + CoT` (single reasoning trace per step, no self-consistency). Optional 3rd arm only if budget allows: `few-shot CoT` (1–3 hand-written exemplars). Self-consistency (k≥5 samples + majority vote) **out of scope** unless requested — it conflates \"CoT\" with \"sampling\". | Which arms are in scope? Self-consistency in/out? Exemplar budget? |\n| c | **WorkArena++ subset** | Stratified subset across difficulty L1/L2/L3 and across the underlying ServiceNow apps (e.g., Knowledge, Catalog, HR, etc.); aim for ≥30 tasks total with proportional L1/L2/L3 split mirroring the full benchmark. Full benchmark deferred to a follow-up. | Full benchmark or subset? Exact stratification rule? Difficulty mix? |\n| d | **Agent loop / action space** | BrowserGym default action space (`bid`, `click`, `type`, `select`, etc.) with the framework's stock system prompt shell (i.e., we modify only the *user/prompt* layer, not the action grammar). Single-turn-then-tool loop, max-step cap per BrowserGym default for WorkArena++. | Where to inject CoT (system vs. user vs. just-before-action)? Custom agent loop allowed? |\n| e | **Trials & seeds** | `n_trials = 3` per (task, condition, model), with task seeds re-rolled per trial by re-instantiating the env and using BrowserGym's deterministic seed. Mean of trials is the per-cell value; report per-trial std. | Number of trials? Seed policy? |\n| f | **Metrics** | Primary: success rate (binary, per WorkArena++ evaluator). Secondary: step count, #failed actions, wall-clock, USD cost (prompt + completion tokens). Tertiary: reasoning-length vs. success scatter. | Which metrics matter? Cost-ceiling? |\n| g | **Evaluator** | WorkArena++ ships with programmatic + (for some tasks) LLM-judge validators; this design treats **only programmatic validators** as ground truth and reports judge-validator agreement as a sensitivity check — never as the primary signal. | Are LLM-judges acceptable as primary? Which judge? |\n\n## 3) Proposed high-level approach (skeleton)\n\n**Research question reframed (operational)**: For LLM-based agents on WorkArena++, does appending a chain-of-thought step before each action increase per-task success rate, after controlling for model identity and task difficulty?\n\n**Conditions (cells)**:\n- `Model ∈ {M_open, M_frontier}` (confirmed or revised in (a)).\n- `Prompt ∈ {ZeroShot, ZeroShot+CoT}` (primary); optional `FewShot+CoT` arm.\n\n**Independent variable**: prompting condition (binary; CoT on/off). `Model` is a stratification factor, not the variable of interest.\n\n**Dependent variables (DVs)**: success rate, mean steps-to-success, mean cost/task, failure rate by task category.\n\n**Controls (held fixed across cells)**:\n- BrowserGym version, ServiceNow instance, action grammar, max-step cap, message-history window.\n- System-prompt preamble, observation truncation, tokenizer settings (`temperature`, `top_p`).\n- Task seeds and environment-internal RNG.\n- Number and ordering of tasks presented to each agent run.\n\n**Randomization**:\n- Task order randomized per run; trial index (`t = 1..3`) is the random seed for env reset.\n- Within a (model, task) cell, the two prompting conditions are run on **the same trial indices** so that any trial-level variance cancels via paired analysis.\n\n**Causal argument for \"CoT helps\"**:\n- **Primary test**: paired difference in success per task between `ZeroShot` and `ZeroShot+CoT` within a fixed model. Use a paired test appropriate to binary outcomes (exact McNemar on the tasks that flip, or a paired Cochran–Armitage-style sign test across tasks). This isolates the prompt change from task identity variance.\n- **Effect size**: report absolute success-rate delta **and** the proportion of tasks that flipped sign (harm/help/no-change) — McNemar alone can be misleading under low base rate.\n- **Disaggregation by L1/L2/L3** to test the theoretically motivated prediction that CoT helps more on harder (L2/L3) tasks.\n- **Confound avoidance**: keep action grammar and observation format identical between arms; if self-consistency/coarse-few-shot is added later, it must be added in a *separate* arm so we never conflate \"CoT\" with \"more compute / more exemplars\".\n\n**Source-supported vs. assumed**:\n- *Source-supported*: nothing about WorkArena++ itself is source-supported here (no docs in workspace); only the general experimental-design primitives (paired designs, McNemar, stratification) are standard.\n- *Assumed*: every numeric default in §2.\n\n## 4) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties\n- **A1. Expected empirical outcome is unknown.** Hypotheses to pre-register before seeing results: (H1) CoT improves overall success rate; (H2) effect is larger on L2/L3; (H3) cost per solved task may rise even with higher success rate. I will not pre-commit here to H1 being true.\n- **A2. Compute / API budget is unstated.** With `n_tasks · n_trials · (2 models) · (2 prompts) = 4·n_tasks·3` episodes per metric cell, even n_tasks=30 yields ~360 episodes per model. Confirm budget; otherwise reduce n_trials to 1 or n_tasks.\n- **A3. Hosted-LLM availability.** No GPU; an open-model baseline therefore requires either a hosted OpenAI-compatible endpoint (network disabled) or acceptance that the open-model arm is \"deferred\". I will **propose** a smarter default: use a single frontier model with two prompting arms as the primary comparison, and make the open-model arm optional.\n- **A4. Action-grammar fidelity.** Confirm the prompt injection point (\"think → act\") is *not* already part of BrowserGym's default prompt; if it is, the \"CoT\" arm needs a syntactic-only change (e.g., add a `Thought:` prefix) rather than a semantically-novel one.\n- **A5. Prompt leakage / contamination.** WorkArena++ tasks live on a public ServiceNow demo; if any backbone model was trained on benchmarks-collected web data, success rates on validation-style tasks may be inflated. I will treat any \"perfect score on a task\" cell as a contamination flag and recommend an *unseen/permutation* sub-check (e.g., reordered form fields).\n- **A6. Non-determinism.** API temperature=0 is not guaranteed identical across vendors (reasoning_effort, sampling params). I will (i) set `temperature=0` where supported, (ii) record provider-version, (iii) require n_trials≥3 and report per-trial variance.\n- **A7. Evaluator variability.** WorkArena++ uses programmatic + LLM-judge validators for some subtasks; using the LLM-judge as primary source introduces a confound when the *same* LLM family is both agent and judge. Mitigation: programmatic-only primary; judge used only as sensitivity analysis; never judge-with-actor.\n- **A8. Truncation / context length.** WorkArena++ DOM observations can exceed 100k tokens; truncation policy is a hidden confounder. Hold fixed between arms, log the truncation rate per cell.\n- **A9. CoT definition is tool-conditional.** I propose \"CoT = one structured `Thought:` block per agent step, before the action token,\" with a fixed schema (intent → relevant observation → predicted next state → action). Deviating from a fixed schema makes \"CoT\" a moving target.\n- **A10. No prior numbers will be cited.** I will not quote WorkArena++ baseline success rates or task counts in this design unless the researcher provides them.\n\n## Top clarifications needed (please confirm before I draft the full design)\n1. **Prompting arms in scope**: confirm the primary contrast is *only* `ZeroShot` vs. `ZeroShot+CoT` (single reasoning trace, no voting). Is self-consistency explicitly out?\n2. **Backbone models**: which model IDs exactly? Is the open-model arm required in this task, or is a single frontier model with two prompting arms acceptable as the primary comparison?\n3. **WorkArena++ subset**: full benchmark, or a stratified subset? Please confirm the L1/L2/L3 task enumeration you want (or hand me the list — none is in the workspace).\n4. **Trials per task**: confi