low-up turn. (3) **WorkArena++ subset policy**: confirm that we will use a **stratified subset** with proportional L1/L2/L3 representation (your proposed ~30 tasks) rather than the full benchmark, AND specify the rule: either (i) replicate the published L1/L2/L3 fraction exactly (you'll need to supply the fractions since they aren't in the workspace), (ii) cap at e.g. 10 tasks per difficulty level for cost control, or (iii) hand-pick a canonical short list (please provide it). Once these three are answered, set approve_approach=true on the next turn and produce the final design document covering: rationale tied to the question, full condition matrix with cell counts, randomization and paired-design mechanics, the exact statistical test (and a power/coverage note for the chosen n_tasks and n_trials), the CoT prompt template (system vs. user injection point and the fixed Thought: schema), controls and confound mitigations (truncation, temperature, contamination check, evaluator policy, judge-actor separation), the analysis plan (primary + secondary + disaggregated by L1/L2/L3), and a feasibility / cost discussion making the assumptions A2 and A3 explicit. Do not cite any WorkArena++ numeric results, task counts, version pins, or baseline rates from memory — if any such number appears, mark it as an assumption pending researcher confirmation. Also do not invent a Research Topic file; treat the missing `neurips2024/97713/3:setup_1` reference as not in scope.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 18}
